              "id": "call_dcO6H8xOd6nJBScAZrw3KWDd",
              "function": {
                "arguments": "{\"page_summary\":\"Wikipedia article 'Alps' lead section and infobox. The visible lead text states that the Alps (/\u00e6lps/) are the highest and most extensive mountain range system that lies entirely in Europe, stretching approximately 1,200 kilometres (750 mi) across eight Alpine countries: Austria, France, Germany, Italy, Liechtenstein, Monaco, Slovenia, and Switzerland. The Caucasus Mountains are higher, and the Uralic longer, but both lie partly in Asia. The mountains were formed over tens of millions of years as the African and Eurasian tectonic plates collided. Extensive shortening caused by the event resulted in marine sedimentary rocks rising by thrusting and folding to high mountain peaks such as Mont Blanc and the Matterhorn. Mont Blanc spans the French-Italian border, and at 4,810 m (15,780 ft) is the highest mountain in the Alps. The Alpine region contains about a hundred peaks higher than 4,000 m (13,123 ft), known as the \\\"four-thousanders\\\". The altitude and size of the ranges affect the climate in Europe; precipitation levels vary greatly and climatic conditions consist of distinct zones. Wildlife such as ibex live in the higher peaks, and plants such as edelweiss grow in rocky areas. Evidence of human habitation in the Alps goes back to the Paleolithic era.\",\"keyfact\":\"Mont Blanc is the highest mountain in the Alps at 4,810 m (15,780 ft).\",\"images\":[{\"image_summary\":\"Photograph captioned \\\"Mont Blanc, the highest mountain in the Alps, view from the Savoy side\\\" showing a snow-covered mountain peak and surrounding ridges under a clear sky.\",\"keyfact\":\"Photograph depicts Mont Blanc and its caption states it is the highest mountain in the Alps.\"}],\"tables\":[{\"table_summary\":\"Infobox titled \\\"Alps\\\" containing a thumbnail of Mont Blanc and data fields. Visible fields: Peak: \\\"Highest point Mont Blanc\\\"; Elevation: \\\"4,810 m (15,780 ft)\\\"; Geography: a Lua/module error message is shown: \\\"Lua error in Module:Location map at line 526: Unable to find the specified location map definition: \\\\\\\"Mountains\\\\\\\". Module:Location_map/data/Alps does not exist.\\\"; Country: \\\"Slovenia\\\"; Orogeny: \\\"Alpine orogeny\\\"; Rock age: \\\"Tertiary\\\"; Rock type: \\\"Basement schist\\\".\",\"keyfact\":\"Infobox lists Mont Blanc as the highest point with elevation 4,810 m (15,780 ft) and shows a location-map Lua error.\"}]}",
                "name": "PageDescription"
              },
              "type": "function"
            }
          ]
        },
